SUMMARY:WIP presentations — Emory Decision-Making Megalab
DESCRIPTION:Works in progress. Works-in-progress presentations from Pete 
 Hitchcock and Michael Hallquist\, with time for discussion and feedback.
  Background papers for Michael’s presentation\, “Free-operant learning\,
  vigor\, and psychopathology\,” are linked with this meeting. No advance
  reading is required. Background reading: Tonic dopamine: Opportunity co
 sts and the control of response vigor. Authors: Niv\, Daw\, Joel & Dayan
 . Journal: Psychopharmacology (2007). Background on average reward rate\
 , the opportunity cost of time\, and response vigor. https://pubmed.ncbi
 .nlm.nih.gov/17031711/ Background reading: On two types of deviation fro
 m the matching law: Bias and undermatching. Authors: Baum. Journal: Jour
 nal of the Experimental Analysis of Behavior (1974). Background on how b
 ehavior is allocated across competing sources of reinforcement. https://
 pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1333261/ Optional background: A compari
 son of variable-ratio and variable-interval schedules of reinforcement. 
 Authors: Zuriff. Journal: Journal of the Experimental Analysis of Behavi
 or (1970). Shows how different reinforcement contingencies can produce d
 ifferent response rates even at equal reinforcement rates. https://pmc.n
 cbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1333678/ Lead: Pete Hitchcock and Michael Ha
 llquist. Location: PAIS 280.
